264	     *  pool is balanced and there is a pot (null: none), a retired or held member cuts 0.00 (their share spread over the others) and each other member's
265	     *  cut is the pot (the sheet's, or for a member pool its cut in the pool above) times their share divided by the
266	     *  shares of the members with a cut, added up, rounded half to even to two decimals, and the pot less the cuts
267	     *  goes to the member with the smallest non-zero cut (the latest added on a tie; a member with no cut gets
268	     *  none, and when no cut is non-zero it goes to the last member with a cut and a share), so the cuts total
269	     *  exactly the pot; when every member is retired there are no cuts ('' shown). A hold or a retirement leaves the total
270	     *  share and balance alone. A member whose membership dates do not include the
271	     *  date is left out entirely: not in the total share, not in the balance, and no cut ('' shown). */
272	    public static PoolResponse from(Pool pool, List<PoolMember> members, Map<Long, LocalDate> retiredFrom,
273	            Set<Long> held, LocalDate on, BigDecimal pot) {
274	        BigDecimal total = BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2);
275	        boolean[] retired = new boolean[members.size()];
276	        boolean[] outside = new boolean[members.size()];
277	        for (int i = 0; i < members.size(); i++) {
278	            PoolMember m = members.get(i);
279	            outside[i] = !m.covers(on);
280	            if (outside[i]) {
